From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: Add the data lane order to the MIPI D-PHY configuration

A DSI host that reads its board's lane order from the data-lanes
property has no way to give it to a separate D-PHY, which is where
MediaTek's lane routing lives. phy_configure_opts_mipi_dphy assumes the
lanes run in order from lane 0.

Add data_lanes, numbered as in DT, from 1. All zero means in order,
which is what every existing caller passes when it zeroes the options.
PHYs that cannot route lanes ignore the field.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 include/linux/phy/phy-mipi-dphy.h |   9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/phy/phy-mipi-dphy.h b/include/linux/phy/phy-mipi-dphy.h
--- a/include/linux/phy/phy-mipi-dphy.h
+++ b/include/linux/phy/phy-mipi-dphy.h
@@ -273,6 +273,15 @@
 	 * lane 0, used for the transmissions.
 	 */
 	unsigned char		lanes;
+
+	/**
+	 * @data_lanes:
+	 *
+	 * Physical data lane that carries each of the @lanes logical
+	 * data lanes, numbered from 1 as in the data-lanes property of
+	 * video-interfaces.yaml. All zero means the lanes are in order.
+	 */
+	unsigned char		data_lanes[4];
 };
 
 int phy_mipi_dphy_get_default_config(unsigned long pixel_clock,
